    "verbatim_sha256": "0af0594c57d8db8c2e3869eac9f256a9b8259403f9fea44a2f4692580d4d7a3d",
    "verbatim": "**Verdict: one distinct custody comparator.** The default portal path reconstructs a loose item in another `ServerLevel` with its original UUID, discards the source without an admission acknowledgment, and immediately attempts a destination merge. EA-0020 covers exposure-driven species replacement. EA-0066 covers Allay pickup and redelivery. Legacy row `6e3238ecb552b7f6385d` already owns the item NBT reader. The distinct evidence here is the cross-level handoff and its admission-to-merge ordering. [EA-0020](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/ecology-availability-research/batch-015.json:21) · [Prior custody comparison](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/ecology-availability-research/general-item-portal-dimension-original-uuid-candidate-20261123.json:239) · [Legacy item reader](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/legacy-migration-acceptance/reviewed.jsonl:262)\n\n- **Gate and restore.** `NetherPortalBlock.java:71–75` and `Entity.java:2048–2087,2546–2548` gate the attempt on portal eligibility, cooldown, and the target level. `Entity.java:2454–2463` exits before source removal on a Forge travel veto or null `PortalInfo`. With a valid exit, the default callback creates the same type in the destination, calls `restoreFrom`, applies portal pose and velocity, and requests admission. `restoreFrom` round-trips source NBT with `Dimension` removed. The base reader restores the UUID, and the item reader restores the stack, age, pickup delay, lifespan, health, and optional owner and thrower. This produces a new Java object with the original UUID. [Entity transfer source](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/tools/cod4/legacy-migration-acceptance/.work/sources/minecraft-forge-1.20.1-47.4.10/net/minecraft/world/entity/Entity.java:2442)\n- **Admission and conversion exits.** `ServerLevel.java:822–824,855–867` shows that `addDuringTeleport` discards the `addEntity` boolean. The join event precedes UUID uniqueness and section insertion (`PersistentEntitySectionManager.java:61–104`). After `placeEntity` returns normally, the original is removed with `CHANGED_DIMENSION`, even if the default factory returned null or destination admission failed (`Entity.java:2465–2494`). A custom teleporter returning null or a non-item replacement also skips the item merge. Its identity and placement behavior require separate evidence. [Admission source spans](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/ecology-availability-research/general-item-portal-dimension-original-uuid-candidate-20261123.json:214)\n- **Immediate merge.** `ItemEntity.java:379–385` calls `mergeWithNeighbours` on the returned item after source removal. The merge uses compatible stacks and matching pickup target, with the larger stack receiving and ties favoring the neighbor (`ItemEntity.java:202–267`). A join veto or duplicate UUID can leave the returned object unadmitted but still eligible to merge, because `isAlive()` checks removal rather than registration. This is a static possibility. Future evidence needs the destination admission result **before** the inline merge, then both participant UUIDs and stack counts. [Item merge source](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/tools/cod4/legacy-migration-acceptance/.work/sources/minecraft-forge-1.20.1-47.4.10/net/minecraft/world/entity/item/ItemEntity.java:202)\n- **Oil CLI boundary.** `dynasty-oil-contact-v1` requires the contact’s world and dimension to equal the origin’s. A cross-level contact yields `contact_not_original_item`. Its lineage schema accepts `merge` and `debit` only, so it cannot represent a portal handoff or prove continuity through a round trip with matching endpoints. [CLI lineage rules](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/ecology-availability-research/general_oil_pickup_audit_20261126.py:105) · [CLI contact binding](/Users/a15356015027/Desktop/dynasty/docs/cod4/audit-20261022/ecology-availability-research/general_oil_pickup_audit_20261126.py:156)\n\nVerified the pinned Forge archive SHA-256 `1b3fbc4e77b7523058b8c03ee4c9f8d9db2a6c9bb41f4afc5277f968ad1070e0` and all 8 members and 28 spans in the prior receipt. Review was offline and read-only, with no historical log review, runtime, or formal intake.",
    "verdict": "One fixed-source candidate, pending Main formal intake."
  },
